## Key Learning

OpenSSH enforces strict ownership and permission requirements for `ChrootDirectory`. Even when user authentication succeeds, an incorrectly 
configured chroot environment causes the SSH daemon to terminate the session immediately, resulting in errors such as **"Connection reset by peer"** 
or **"Broken pipe"**. Following a structured troubleshooting approach—starting with network validation and progressing through SSH debugging and 
configuration review—helps identify the root cause efficiently and minimise production downtime.

